	regionKind = "dungeon",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Razorfen Kraul is the great thorn warren of the {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link} at the southern edge of {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link}, near the border of {link:thousand-needles}Thousand Needles{/link}. It is a maze of trenches, tunnels and bridges woven through thorn vines so vast that they rise like walls around it. The quilboar hold it sacred. It is also a fortress, and in the present day it is the seat of a crone who means to make the southern Barrens her own.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[Ten thousand years ago, in the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}, the demigod {red:agamaggan}Agamaggan{/red} rose to fight the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}. The great boar fell in battle. His body flattened the land where he died, and his blood sank into the earth. Where it fell, twisted spires of thorns grew up. The {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link}, who call themselves his children, came to dwell among the thorns and named them the Razorfen. The Kraul is one of their greatest strongholds.

The night elves remember Agamaggan as a pure and generous being. Their druids cannot say why the land around his resting place has become so foul, nor why the thorns seem to spread a corruption of their own.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The old crone {link:charlga-razorflank}Charlga Razorflank{/link} rules the Kraul. She is a mistress of earth magic, and she is gathering an army. Under the {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link} of the southern {link:the-barrens}Barrens{/link}, the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} were driven from lands they had held for generations, and they have not forgotten it. From the Kraul came the three {link:razormane-quilboar}Razormane{/link} leaders who bled the supply lines of the {link:the-crossroads}Crossroads{/link} from {link:blackthorn-ridge}Blackthorn Ridge{/link}.

Worse is rumored. A letter taken from the crone bears the seal of the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}. An envoy of the undead waits outside {link:razorfen-downs}Razorfen Downs{/link}, the other great warren to the east, and offers her the Barrens and more in exchange for a free hand. Her warriors already speak of new allies.

Few outsiders have entered the Kraul and come out again. A {link:night-elves}night elf{/link} druid named {link:heralath-fallowbrook}Heralath{/link} and a {link:dwarves}dwarf{/link} of the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} were dragged here as prisoners. A goblin trader came for rare tubers and was caught. Now the alarm has reached {link:thalanaar}Thalanaar{/link}, {link:thunder-bluff}Thunder Bluff{/link} and even the {link:undercity}Undercity{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Within the Kraul",
			text = [=[• {b}The Trenches.{/b} Winding paths below the thorns, where blueleaf tubers grow and beast trainers keep their boars.
• {b}The Overlord's Hall.{/b} {link:overlord-ramtusk}Overlord Ramtusk{/link} commands the war host here, with the {link:death-speaker-jargba}Death Speaker Jargba{/link} and the prophet {link:aggem-thorncurse}Aggem Thorncurse{/link} nearby.
• {b}The Bat Caves.{/b} Deep tunnels full of Kraul bats. In their darkest depths hunts a pale beast that has never seen daylight.
• {b}The Pen.{/b} A tunnel sealed by a barrier of {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link} magic, where {link:agathelos-the-raging}Agathelos the Raging{/link} is kept.
• {b}The Crone's Hut.{/b} Charlga's dwelling stands high on a ramp of thorns. Below it, in a small hut, lie the prisoners of the Kraul.]=],
		},
	},
})

